++<h1>How to Rotate PDF Pages Free — Fix Upside-Down or Sideways Pages</h1>
++<p>Scanned a document the wrong way up? Got a PDF where some pages are landscape and others are portrait? Rotating PDF pages takes seconds — no software needed, no upload required.</p>
++
++<div class="cta-box"><p>Rotate PDF pages free — no upload, no account</p><a href="https://rightpdfkit.com/#rotate" class="cta-btn">Rotate PDF Free →</a></div>
++
++<h2>How to rotate PDF pages — step by step</h2>
++<ol>
++  <li>Open the <strong>Rotate PDF</strong> tool on RightPDFKit.</li>
++  <li>Upload your PDF by dragging it in or clicking to browse.</li>
++  <li>A thumbnail view of all pages appears. Click any page to select it, or use <strong>Select All</strong> to rotate every page at once.</li>
++  <li>Choose your rotation: <strong>90° clockwise</strong>, <strong>90° counter-clockwise</strong>, or <strong>180° (flip upside-down)</strong>.</li>
++  <li>Click <strong>Save &amp; Download</strong>.</li>
++</ol>
++
++<h2>Can I rotate just one page?</h2>
++<p>Yes. Click the thumbnail of the specific page you want to rotate, apply the rotation, and the rest of the document stays unchanged. This is useful when a scan has one portrait page in the middle of a landscape document.</p>
++
++<h2>Does rotation permanently fix the PDF?</h2>
++<p>Yes. The rotation is written into the PDF file — it's not just a view setting. When you download and open the file in any PDF reader (Adobe Reader, Preview, Chrome, your phone), the pages will be correctly oriented.</p>
++<p>This is different from rotating a page in your browser's PDF viewer, which only adjusts the view temporarily and reverts when you close the tab.</p>
++
++<h2>Why do PDFs have rotated pages?</h2>
++<ul>
++  <li><strong>Phone or scanner orientation</strong> — photographing a document while holding your phone sideways</li>
++  <li><strong>Mixed-orientation documents</strong> — a wide table scanned in landscape inserted into a portrait document</li>
++  <li><strong>Incorrect export settings</strong> — some Word or LibreOffice exports flip the orientation</li>
++  <li><strong>Merged PDFs</strong> — combining files that were created in different orientations</li>
++</ul>
++
++<h2>Rotate before sharing or uploading</h2>
++<p>If you're submitting a document to a government portal, HR system or university application, always check page orientation first. Upside-down pages can cause automatic document processing systems to fail or reject the upload entirely.</p>
