++<h1>How to Convert PDF to Excel Free — No Upload, No Account</h1>
++<p>Stuck with a PDF full of tables you need to edit in a spreadsheet? You can extract tables directly from a PDF and get an editable Excel or CSV file — without uploading your document anywhere.</p>
++
++<div class="cta-box"><p>Convert PDF to Excel free — no upload, no account</p><a href="https://rightpdfkit.com/#pdf-to-excel" class="cta-btn">PDF to Excel Free →</a></div>
++
++<h2>How to convert PDF to Excel — step by step</h2>
++<ol>
++  <li>Open the <strong>PDF to Excel</strong> tool on RightPDFKit.</li>
++  <li>Upload your PDF — drag it in or click to browse.</li>
++  <li>The tool detects tables automatically. Preview the extracted data before downloading.</li>
++  <li>Choose your output format: <strong>.xlsx</strong> for Excel, or <strong>.csv</strong> for Google Sheets or any other tool.</li>
++  <li>Click <strong>Download</strong>.</li>
++</ol>
