++  <tr><td>PDF with simple, clean grid tables</td><td class="good">✓ Very good</td></tr>
++  <tr><td>PDF with merged cells or complex headers</td><td style="color:#e67e22;font-weight:700">◎ Good, may need minor cleanup</td></tr>
++  <tr><td>Scanned PDF (image of a document)</td><td class="bad">✗ Needs OCR first</td></tr>
++</table>
++<p>For scanned PDFs, use the <a href="ocr-extract-text-scanned-pdf.html">OCR tool</a> first to make the text selectable, then convert to Excel.</p>
++
++<h2>PDF to Excel vs copying and pasting</h2>
++<p>Manually copying tables from a PDF into Excel is tedious and error-prone — especially for multi-page tables or documents with dozens of rows. The converter extracts all tables at once, preserving row and column structure, so you don't have to reformat anything.</p>
++
